## Overview

Arachne is one of Marathon’s six playable factions.{{cite:techradar-launch}} GamesRadar describes Arachne as a mysterious death cult focused on the thermodynamics of violence.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} GamesRadar states Arachne manifests as a PvP-focused faction in-game.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Arachne’s agent is named Charter and is said to encourage killing other Runners.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## What Arachne offers Runners

Players can gain Arachne reputation by completing Arachne contracts.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} GamesRadar lists rank-up rewards including non-chip weapon mods and Arachne salvage items and weapons.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} GamesRadar lists the Armory offerings from Arachne as weapons, mods, and implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Bungie’s Server Slam allowed players to progress through early Arachne faction levels and progression trees.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Players can also earn Arachne reputation by exfiling with a Tag Chip.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Recent changes and tuning

Update 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026) increased starting ammo in Arachne free Sponsored Kits.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Season 2 reworked Priority Contracts to focus on loot and removed faction-reputation gating for them.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie added new Season 2 implant and chip content and other tuning coming with the season.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Ranked matches include Tag Chips as loot that auto-sell on exfil and contribute score.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

