## Overview

Sekiguchi Genetics is one of Marathon’s six factions.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Sekiguchi develops the biomata Runner shells grown by WEAVEworms.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The company uses an AI agent named Nona to pursue shell research and experiments.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## Role and offerings

Sekiguchi grants rank-up rewards such as cores, Sekiguchi salvage, and head implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Sekiguchi’s armory stocks Marathon cores, an Energy Amp consumable, and implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Players gain Sekiguchi reputation by completing Sekiguchi contracts and looting specific Sekiguchi valuables.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## Progression and seasonal context

Full progression for all six factions, including Sekiguchi Genetics, was promised during Season 1 content plans.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} All six factions, Sekiguchi included, were listed as available at launch.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Seasonal updates can add faction upgrades, contracts, and other faction content.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Season 2's Cradle system changes Runner shell stats and progression shared across shells.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Recent fixes and tuning

Bungie noted implant presentation and usability problems during Season 1 tuning feedback.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

