## Overview

Vandal’s archetype is described as a Combat anarchist.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Vandal shells traverse ground at incredible speeds using advanced movement and a knockback cannon.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Bungie released a Vandal Shell cinematic as part of Season 2 promotional materials.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}}

## Abilities and Playstyles

Players can customize Vandal playstyle through cores, implants, weapons, and mods.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Vandal can be built for extreme mobility by equipping cores that convert double jump into a triple jump.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Implants can increase Vandal’s base movement speed, jump height, and heat capacity.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} An alternate Vandal build uses the arm cannon as a self-propel mechanic by firing downward to launch upward.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Using that arm-cannon propulsion, Vandals can use airtime to position and then deal area damage on landing without taking fall damage.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Runner shells, including Vandal, have customizable kits that change how their archetypes are played.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## Notable Changes and Rewards

Season 2 Bungie Rewards require exfiltrating as Vandal to claim the Renaissance Runner Codex Challenge.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

