## Archetype

Thief's archetype is described as covert acquisitions.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Thief is the sixth Runner shell.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie lists Thief among the six launch Runner shells.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}

## Abilities and Design

Thief shells use enhanced visors and a piloted butterfly drone to locate and acquire loot.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Thief shells have a grapple device to push an advantage or make an escape.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} One Thief core can grant a second charge of the Grapple Device.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Another Thief core makes the Pickpocket Drone periodically ping nearby enemies when not piloted.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Notable changes and rollout

Thief did not participate in the Server Slam playtest but was planned to be available at launch.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} A Thief Shell cinematic is listed among other shell cinematics in Bungie's Season 2 materials.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}} An update fixed duplicated Thief voice over lines in the Russian language (Update 1.1.0.1, June 9, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}}

