## Mod slots and chips

Weapons have three or four mod slots for attachments like optics, magazines, barrels, and grips.{{cite:gamesradar-weapons}} Every weapon has a single chip slot reserved for a chip that grants an extra weapon perk.{{cite:gamesradar-weapons}}

## Chips and new chip families

Season 2 adds eight new chips to the game.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Examples of Season 2 chips include Brain Freeze, Alarmist, and Scrapyard chips.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie described chips as the software upgrades that enable notable weapon behavior changes.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

## Folding stock

Folding Stocks are a new Season 2 mod family that alter weapon gameplay via a unique action.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} The KKV-9SD and the D54 Battle Pistol are the first weapons to gain Folding Stocks.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Using the Folding Stock lets players keep it closed for hip-fire benefits or unfold it for ADS benefits.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Prestige mods and tuning

Prestige weapon mods exist and their drop chances were slightly reduced in Update 1.1.0.1 (June 9, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}} Season 2 adjusted existing Prestige mods such as reducing Full-Auto Selector's rate of fire bonus.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} The KKV-9SD's Prestige mod Flechette Drum heals the player when breaking a hostile's shield.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Patch notes fixed issues related to specific Prestige mods, including the D54 Battle Pistol's Daredevil Stock (Update 1.1.0.1, June 9, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}}

