## Setting

Perimeter is an edge-site expansion on the colony's outskirts.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie describes Perimeter as a beginner-friendly map set on the colony's edges.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} Perimeter is one of Marathon's three surface zones alongside Dire Marsh and Outpost.{{cite:bungie-vidoc}} Perimeter originally supported five-crew matches at launch.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## Layout highlights

The Symbiosis update adds two major playable spaces: the underground Burrows and the submerged Reservoir.{{cite:bungie-press-symbiosis}} Symbiosis-era Perimeter features a fungal ecosystem that opens new paths through the map.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Perimeter contains unique high-difficulty activity territory where the Tick Queen can be encountered.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Access and rules

Perimeter was playable during the Server Slam preview event before launch.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Sponsored Perimeter rotations have been scheduled on weekends during live events and updates.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Perimeter is included in Expedition runs as a selectable zone with scaling difficulty.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Notable changes

Nightfall Refresh announced a future expansion of Perimeter in December under the Symbiosis roadmap.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Bungie revealed Symbiosis will launch on December 8, 2026, and includes the updated Perimeter.{{cite:bungie-press-symbiosis}} Update 1.1.9.7 listed Sponsored Survival: Perimeter available through November 17, 2026.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} Update 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026) increased med cabinet and munitions crate spawns on Perimeter.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}}

