## Setting

Night Marsh is a pitch-black version of Dire Marsh introduced in Season 2.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}} The zone plays slower and leans toward survival horror with extra environmental navigation challenges.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Anomaly energy flows from Complex, affecting staircases and closed doors leading to upper Complex areas.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Layout and mechanics highlights

Upper Complex on Night Marsh contains locked rooms with rarer loot and mysteries behind UESC-encrypted doors.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Network Towers can be hacked with UESC encryption certificates called Certs to access stockpiles and exfils.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Complex Control contains staircases to upper rooms that require Certs to open for investigation and loot.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Anomalous activities like the Anomaly obscure long sight lines and alter navigation in the dark.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Darkness tools and combat changes

All Runners gain access to flashlights on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Darksight Scopes add a night-vision toggle while aiming down sights to reveal the surrounding environment.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Vector Grenades produce lingering revealing pulses that highlight areas and enemies and are essential on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Signal Flares in three colors provide lingering light and non-verbal communication options.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

## Access rules and availability

Night Marsh and Dire Marsh are both available continuously for the first week of Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} After the first week, Night Marsh and Dire Marsh rotate availability with one another every 90 minutes.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Night Marsh unlocks at Runner Level 3 for players who did not complete Dire Marsh previously.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Sponsored Night Marsh events recur on a schedule during special events and updates.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

## Notable changes and mode integration

Expedition Phase 1 includes Night Marsh as a playable zone for its roguelite PvE runs.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} The Critical Incident in Expedition can include solving Upper Complex activity on Night Marsh.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Season 2 introduced Night Marsh alongside new Runner shell Sentinel and multiple sandbox updates.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}}

