## Setting

Cryo Archive is the first deck of the UESC Marathon, an abandoned ship hanging in orbit with cryopods, medical bays, and storage wings.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The deck is described as a frozen snapshot of the past promising valuable resources and information.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Layout and features

Cryo Archive consists of six interconnected wings arranged around a central hub.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The zone contains seven heavily secured Vaults that require specific Vault Keys and entry challenges.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Tight corridors open into large spaces designed to pit enemy crews against each other to unseal Vaults.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Access rules and progression

Players must meet Runner Level 25, have all six factions unlocked, and a 5,000 credit Loadout Value to queue.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Security Clearance is built during a run and gates systems like doors, supply rooms, and exfils by level.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Vault Keys can be found planet‑side, on the ship, and from downed enemy Runner crews.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} When available, a pool of seven Cryo contracts appears in CyberAcme and completing a contract removes it from the weekly pool.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Each completed Cryo contract gives a random high‑rarity item, and Codex progression for Cryo Archive persists between weeks.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Notable changes and schedule

Cryo Archive originally opened on weekends starting Friday, March 20.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Season 2 reworked Cryo contracts to allow progress over multiple runs and kept the seventh contract tied to the Compiler.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} During the Nightfall Refresh, Cryo Archive ran weekly from Thursday through Monday starting October 15 under an improved schedule.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Vault Breaker is an experimental roguelite PvE mode set inside Cryo Archive introduced in mid‑Season 2.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}} A bug in Vault 4 that could trap players was fixed in Update 1.1.9.7 (November 10, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026) changed Cryo Archive Armory offerings and Vault Key availability during the Vault Breaker event window.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

