## Priority contracts

Priority Contracts are one-time missions that are central to a faction’s narrative and offer superior rewards.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Priority Contracts were described as primary ways the story unfolds and serve like levels or chapters.{{cite:marathonwiki-com-priority-contracts}} In Expedition mode players can complete Priority Contracts while running the PvE series.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Standard and Liaison contracts

Standard contracts are repeatable single-objective challenges that grant basic faction rewards and reputation.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Players are limited to one active contract at a time, and contract progress is shared with crew members.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Liaison contracts must be completed to unlock a faction for earning reputation and taking its other contracts.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Season 2 refreshed Standard and Liaison contracts to reduce onerous requirements and rough edges.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} If a player completed a faction’s Liaison contracts in Season 1, that faction remains unlocked for Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 increased faction reputation gains from Standard Contracts and reduced some material costs for upgrades.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Cryo Archive contracts

When Cryo Archive is active, seven unique Cryo contracts appear in CyberAcme for players to choose from.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Players can re-roll which Cryo contract is active so crews work toward the same objective during a run.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Completing a Cryo contract removes it from a player’s weekly pool, which fully resets when the Archive returns.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Each Cryo contract completion awards a random high-rarity item such as a Vault key, material, or piece of gear.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive runs feature tense puzzle interactions, racing other crews for high-tier containers and unique weapon lockers.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Season 2 reworked Cryo Archive contracts to allow progress across multiple runs and to teach Cryo mechanics, with the seventh contract still requiring defeating the Compiler.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Season 2 contract system changes

Season 2 moved Runner shell upgrades into the Cradle, freeing faction trees and expanding Armory offerings.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Priority Contracts are now focused more on loot rewards and are no longer gated behind faction reputation levels.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 introduced the Cradle to let players change stat focus anytime without needing to level a faction.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie aimed to make contract completion feel more organic and less linear in Season 2.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

