## Overview

Ranked tests looting, PvP, and risk management with score-based progression using Holotags.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Ranked was in beta during Season 1 and first ran March 21–24, 2026.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Players climb six ranks: Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum, Diamond, and Pinnacle, each with three tiers.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Holotags and entry rules

Each Holotag sets a run's score target and loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Holotags persist after exfil and can be sold for full value after exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} You can purchase Holotags up to your current rank tier in the Armory.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Season 2 requires players to bring a Holotag that matches their current rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 combines Low and High Stakes into a single queue with a 5,000 Loadout value minimum.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Scoring and loot

Your team's combined Holotag value decides the score target for a run.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Starting loadouts do not count toward the score target.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} You must exfil at or above the score target to earn Ranked Points; exfiling below yields no RP change.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Looting enemy Holotags or Tag Chips grants overperformance capacity to earn bonus RP above the target.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Loss penalties apply only when a team fails to exfil; the penalty equals the combined Holotag value.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Bronze Holotags have a score target of 3,000 and a loss penalty of 600.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Silver Holotags have a score target of 5,000 and a loss penalty of 2,000.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Gold Holotags have a score target of 7,000 and a loss penalty of 4,200.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Platinum Holotags have a score target of 10,000 and a loss penalty of 8,000.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Diamond Holotags have a score target of 15,000 and a loss penalty of 15,000.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Pinnacle Holotags have a score target of 20,000 and a loss penalty of 20,000.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Tag Chips found in-run count as loot, grant overperformance capacity, and auto-sell on exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Season 2 changes

Ranked returned in Season 2 on June 14 with new rewards.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 adjusted progression to be faster and modified win/loss point changes by average match rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 added a daily Ranked Sponsored Kit containing a loadout appropriate for a player's rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

