## Overview

Bungie introduced the Cradle as a new Season 2 system to give players more control over Runner shell strengths and weaknesses.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}

Season 2’s launch materials list the Cradle as the place to improve Runner shell stats across the season.{{cite:bungie-season-2-live}}

## How the Cradle Works

The Cradle uses WEAVEworms to create biocybernetic bodies and increase Runner shell stats across six categories.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Players convert weapons, equipment, and other items into experience for the Cradle using the Matter Converter.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Leveling the Cradle grants Energy that can be allocated to any of the six stat categories.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Allocated Energy can be reallocated at any time without penalties or limitations.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Cradle progression is shared across all Runner shells and resets at the start of a new season.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Related Systems and Design

Implants were reworked in Season 2 to be defined by a single fixed perk with a matching name and fixed stat package.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Bungie moved Runner shell upgrades from faction progression trees into the Cradle to centralize shell improvements.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} With shell upgrades centralized, faction trees were expanded to offer more Armory options and unique implant families.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Future and Reworks

In October, Bungie reset progression and restored Cradle enhancements and faction aftermarket upgrades to defaults as part of a refresh.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Bungie plans a refactored Cradle and deeper shell progression as part of March’s larger roadmap of connected systems.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} December’s Symbiosis update will add permanent PvE, an expanded Perimeter, a new shell, and improved onboarding before March’s integration.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}}

