## Overview

The Armory offers purchasable Holotags using Credits for Ranked queues.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Season 2 moved many Runner shell upgrades into the Cradle, which allowed the Armory options to expand.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## What the Armory Sells and Barters

CyberAcme's Armory offerings include basic weapons, backpacks, ammo, healing consumables, and keys.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} NuCaloric's Armory offerings include healing consumables, self-revives, shields, and implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Traxus's Armory offerings emphasize weapons and a wide range of mods.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Certain Schemas can now unlock specific Barter offers in the Armory.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Sponsored Kits and Ranked

Season 2 introduced a daily Ranked Sponsored Kit that supplies a loadout scaled to a player's rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} In Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026), Weapon and Backpack Schema wares in the Armory began costing Credits.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} In Update 1.1.9.7 (November 10, 2026), MIDA and Traxus Armory Deluxe sponsored kit weekly stock was reduced and their Superior sponsored kits were removed.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} At the start of Season 2, players received CyberAcme Sponsored Kits based on their Season 1 Runner Level, from an Enhanced kit at level 10 to a Deluxe kit at level 50 and a Superior kit at level 75.{{cite:kotaku-season-2}} Ranked requires a Holotag in the backpack to queue, which can be purchased from the Armory for Credits.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Cryo Archive Sponsored Kit

Players meeting Cryo Archive requirements become eligible for a one-time Cryo Archive Sponsored Kit from the Armory.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The Cryo Archive Sponsored Kit is a blue-tier bundle tuned for an early Cryo Archive run.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

