## Overview

Expedition is a fully PvE cooperative roguelite mode introduced in Symbiosis Phase 1.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Expedition has a dedicated queue across Perimeter, Night Marsh, Outpost, and Cryo Archive.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Players can join Expedition solo, as a duo, or in full trios.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Expedition runs exclude PvP threats so crews face only PvE combat.{{cite:bungie-press-symbiosis}}

## Run Series

Each Expedition session consists of a Run Series of three runs with escalating difficulty.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} The third run is the Critical Incident, where players may adjust difficulty for better rewards.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Players can roll a completed Run Series into a new one to attempt further progression.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Buildcrafting, Flash Boosts, and Run Kits

Expedition introduces Flash Boosts as an in-run upgrade system that shapes builds during a run.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Flash Boosts are looted, earned from defeating tough foes or completing objectives, and can be stacked to upgrade rarity and potency.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Each faction provides a locked faction loadout per Run Series, which can be looted into or improved during runs.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Faction upgrades unlock over progression to improve starting faction loadouts across a series.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} Flash Boosts and in-run gear are sold when a Run Series completes, while credits and XP persist.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}}

## Release and Events

An Open Play Week runs December 8–15, allowing everyone to try Expedition at no cost during that period.{{cite:bungie-symbiosis-open-play}} The Crew Up event runs December 8 to December 22 and integrates Expedition challenges for cooperative rewards.{{cite:bungie-symbiosis-open-play}}

