## Overview

Cores are generally designed for one specific Runner shell and tend to buff or modify how that shell's abilities work.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Players combine cores with implants, weapons, and mods to customize each Runner shell's playstyle.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## How cores change abilities

One Thief core grants a second charge of the Grapple Device.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Another Thief core makes the Pickpocket Drone periodically ping nearby enemies when not piloted.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} A Vandal core can turn double jump into a triple jump to emphasize mobility.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} A Vandal combination can convert the arm cannon into a self-propel that launches the shell and deals area damage on landing.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Seasonal and faction context

Marathon launch content includes cores among other loot such as weapons, mods, and implants.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Seasonal updates can add new cores alongside weapons, mods, implants, and Runner shells.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Season 2 adds a full suite of ten Sentinel-specific Runner cores across rarity tiers.{{cite:bungie-s2-combat-tuning}} Sekiguchi Genetics' Armory offerings include Marathon Cores.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## Acquisition and rewards

Server Slam progression rewards include Standard Runner shell cores in the Standard Arrival Cache.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Enhanced and Deluxe Arrival Caches during Server Slam include Enhanced and Deluxe Runner shell cores respectively.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} GamesRadar compares powerful chip mods' transformative effects on guns to Marathon Cores for Runner shells.{{cite:gamesradar-weapons}}

