## Overview

Tau Ceti IV is a restricted, derelict colony world central to Marathon’s extraction-survival gameplay.{{cite:marathon-official-site}} The planet’s surface data is incomplete and derived from fragmented transmissions and recovered field records.{{cite:marathon-official-site}}

## New Cascadia Colony and the UESC Marathon

The UESC Marathon left Mars in 2472 carrying 30,000 colonists bound for a new home.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} The ship arrived about 300 years later and then contact with the colonists was lost.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The derelict Marathon remains abandoned in orbit and promises valuable resources and information.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive is the Marathon ship’s end-game deck featuring cryopods, medical bays, and Vaults with powerful loot.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## The Vanished Colonists

Thirty thousand people from the New Cascadia colony mysteriously disappeared, forming Marathon’s central mystery.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}}

## Runners and Runner Shells

Players inhabit moddable biosynthetic Runner shells that house transferred consciousnesses for disposable runs.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Each Runner shell centers on an archetype such as intel gathering, disruption, or combat healing.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} Runner shells provide Prime and Tactical abilities, traits, and distinct playstyles for squad roles.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}}

## Zones, Seasons, and Gameplay

Season 1 centers on a gold rush and faction proxy war as Runners seek answers about the New Cascadia disappearance.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Cryo Archive opened for play on weekends starting March 20 and requires a three-player crew plus set progression thresholds.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## When the expedition went dark

Bungie's own materials give different spans for how long the Marathon has been silent.{{cite:marathon-official-site}}{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

