## Overview

The ship left Mars in 2472 and arrived 300 years later before contact was lost.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The original expedition carried 30,000 colonists bound to found a new home.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Silence and Mystery

No one knows what happened when the Marathon expedition went dark a century ago.{{cite:marathon-official-site}} Decades later the ship remains abandoned in orbit as a frozen snapshot of the past.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Cryo Archive Deck

Cryo Archive consists of six interconnected wings arranged around a central hub.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive runs use Security Clearance progression built during a single run to access systems.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The deck contains seven heavily secured Vaults with unique entry challenges and Vault Keys required.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## What Runners Encounter

Players will fight UESC security forces and enemy Runner crews aboard the Marathon.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Vaults contain high-tier containers, materials, top-end equipment, and unique gold weapons.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive emphasizes raid-style puzzle solving, layered mechanics, and high extraction stakes.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Cryo Archive was designed for three-player crews but supports solo queue with fill.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Vault Breaker is a roguelite PvE mode set within Cryo Archive and playable solo, duo, or trio.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}}

## When the expedition went dark

Bungie's own materials give different spans for how long the Marathon has been silent.{{cite:marathon-official-site}}{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

